From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: win32u: a menu bar is painted with its MIM_BACKGROUND brush

Windows paints a menu bar's background with the brush SetMenuInfo(
MIM_BACKGROUND) gave it -- programs with a dark theme draw their bar's
items themselves on a dark background that way. win32u ignored it and
filled the bar with COLOR_MENU / COLOR_MENUBAR, so the bar stayed light
behind a dark program's own items. The bar and the line under it are now
filled with the brush when there is one; without one nothing changes.

Gate: test/notepad-print-gate.sh (Notepad's dark theme: the bar's pixels).
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/menu.c b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
index f232585..b12c85e 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/menu.c
@@ -2736,11 +2736,23 @@ DWORD WINAPI NtUserDrawMenuBarTemp( HWND hwnd, HDC hdc, RECT *rect, HMENU handle
 
     rect->bottom = rect->top + menu->Height;
 
-    fill_rect( hdc, rect, get_sys_color_brush( flat_menu ? COLOR_MENUBAR : COLOR_MENU ));
+    /* a menu bar with a background brush (SetMenuInfo MIM_BACKGROUND) is
+     * painted with it, as on Windows -- dark-themed programs rely on it --
+     * the line under it too */
+    if (menu->hbrBack)
+    {
+        RECT line = { rect->left, rect->bottom, rect->right, rect->bottom + 1 };
+        fill_rect( hdc, rect, menu->hbrBack );
+        fill_rect( hdc, &line, menu->hbrBack );
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        fill_rect( hdc, rect, get_sys_color_brush( flat_menu ? COLOR_MENUBAR : COLOR_MENU ));
 
-    NtGdiSelectPen( hdc, get_sys_color_pen( COLOR_3DFACE ));
-    NtGdiMoveTo( hdc, rect->left, rect->bottom, NULL );
-    NtGdiLineTo( hdc, rect->right, rect->bottom );
+        NtGdiSelectPen( hdc, get_sys_color_pen( COLOR_3DFACE ));
+        NtGdiMoveTo( hdc, rect->left, rect->bottom, NULL );
+        NtGdiLineTo( hdc, rect->right, rect->bottom );
+    }
 
     if (menu->nItems)
     {
